# /sdd-plan

Purpose:
  Scan .sdd/ and prompts/ directories ONCE to generate an execution plan,
  then serve it from cache. Idempotent: 100 invocations = 1 real scan
  + 99 cache hits. Produces a trace-format plan matching the 16-step
  SDDRA execution trace, plus today's work, history context, and
  phase/layer position.

Owns: commands/sdd-plan.sdd

Description:
  Cache-first plan generation command. On cache HIT (fingerprint match),
  serves the plan from .sdd/plans/current-plan.sdd with zero scanning.
  On cache MISS or --replan, performs a single full scan (project metadata,
  chain graph, task registry, phase registry, pending prompts, history,
  git log), writes the plan to .sdd/plans/current-plan.sdd, bumps the
  plan revision, and records the execution in .claude/sdd/history.json.

Usage:
  /sdd-plan
  /sdd-plan --replan
  /sdd-plan --chains
  /sdd-plan --prompts
  /sdd-plan --tasks
  /sdd-plan --full

Options:
  --replan    Force cache regeneration (full rescan, revision bump)
  --chains    Focus on chain arm analysis
  --prompts   Focus on pending prompt classification
  --tasks     Focus on task-to-decision mapping
  --full      Generate complete plan (default)

CacheMechanism:
  CacheFile: .claude/sdd/plan-cache.json
  PlanFile: .sdd/plans/current-plan.sdd

InitialLoad (Phase 151 — EXPAND protocol):
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing only)
  - .claude/sdd/plan-cache.json (fingerprint check)
  - .sdd/plans/current-plan.sdd (cache HIT path: this is the whole load)
  Everything else is EXPAND-only; a cache HIT MUST NOT load any more files.
  FingerprintInputs:
    - git HEAD commit hash
    - .sdd/projects/sddra/tasks/INDEX.sdd state
    - .sdd/projects/sddra/phases/INDEX.sdd state
    - .sdd/projects/sddra/context/active.sdd state
    - prompts/inbox/ new file existence
  HitBehavior:
    - Increment hit_count (only write)
    - Output plan from current-plan.sdd
    - NO rescan of .sdd/, decisions, or git log
  MissBehavior:
    - Full scan ONCE
    - Write plan, bump Revision vN
    - Update fingerprint, reset hit_count
    - Append execution record to .claude/sdd/history.json

ScanSteps (MISS only):
  1: Read .sdd/PROJECT.sdd → extract project name, domain, stack
  2: Read .sdd/plans/current-plan.sdd → prior plan (revision diff)
  3: Read .sdd/projects/sddra/tasks/INDEX.sdd → task states (today filter)
  4: Read .sdd/projects/sddra/phases/INDEX.sdd → phase registry → current phase + layer
  5: Read .sdd/chains/graph.sdd → execution trace and arms
  6: Read .sdd/decisions/INDEX.sdd → active decisions
  7: Scan prompts/inbox/ → pending user requests
     - Tag each prompt with likely chain arm by keywords:
       "write/plan/design" → D1 (docs)
       "implement/code/build" → C1 (code)
       "review/audit/test" → R1 (review)
       "deploy/release" → DEP1 (deploy)
       "analyze/explain" → P1 (prompt)
       "spec/define" → S1 (.sdd)
  8: Read .claude/sdd/history.json → last 3-5 execution records
  9: Query git log --oneline -10 (read-only) → map commits to tasks
  10: Build plan sections:
      a. Project Header (name, domain, stack, counts, current phase)
      b. Today's Work (tasks + inbox + phases)
      c. Execution Trace #01-#16
      d. Phase / Layer Position (phase, layer, flow position D0->arm->D0)
      e. History Context (recent sessions)
      f. Next Action (+ /sdd-next guidance)
  11: Compute new fingerprint → save to plan-cache.json

RePlanProtocol:
  trigger: user requests any plan change
  behavior:
    - Read current-plan.sdd (no rescan)
    - Apply change to plan content
    - Bump Revision (MINOR: task changes; MAJOR: goal/scope changes)
    - Append {command: "/sdd-plan --replan", reason: <user request>} to history.json
    - Output diff summary: what changed, why, new revision
  rule: user edits are plan-local — never trigger full rescans

ChangeMode (adopted 2026-09-13, Phase 152/F):
  BIG: multi-chain/architecture-touching changes — full 16-trace
    plan + phase registry review + DEC record before execution
  SMALL: single-component/single-rule changes — fast-path planning
    per chains/fast-path.sdd (reduced trace, same gates for
    irreversible actions)
  classification: the plan states its mode explicitly; mode drives
    plan depth, never gate strength (L4 irreversible gates always fire)
  source: .sdd/docs/analysis/garry-tan-gstack-alignment.md

Output:
  ```
  # Project: <name> | Domain: <domain> | Stack: <stack>
  # Active Decisions: <count> | Pending Tasks: <count> | Phase: <phase>
  # [cache: HIT #<n> | MISS → rev <N>]

  Today's Work:
    1. [DONE] <item>
    2. [IN_PROGRESS] <item>
    ...

  Execution Plan:
    #01  Discover    -> [EXISTING/.sdd/PROJECT.sdd] - <summary>
    #02  BuildCtx    -> [AUTO] cache-first: plan-cache.json => no rescan
    #03  Plan        -> [TASK/tsk-XXX] - <description>
    #04  PlanCheck   -> [AUTO] validate DAG + dependencies
    #05  Implement   -> [CODE/.sdd/skills/] - <summary>
    #06  Test        -> [CODE/.sdd/testing/] - <summary>
    #07  TestCheck   -> [AUTO] PASS or FAIL branch
    #08  Classify    -> [AUTO] map failure types
    #09  Fix         -> [TASK/tsk-XXX] - <description>
    #10  LoopGuard   -> [AUTO] evaluate loop score + failure budget
    #11  ReTest      -> [AUTO] re-run affected tests
    #12  DoneProof   -> [AUTO] verify requirements + tests + arch + review
    #13  Document    -> [DOCS/.sdd/docs/] - <summary>
    #14  LearnGate   -> [AUTO] evaluate learning gate outcome
    #15  Consolidate -> [AUTO] DROP | ARCHIVE | LINK | PROMOTE knowledge
    #16  Complete    -> [AUTO] mark task COMPLETED

  Phase/Layer: <phase> | Layer: <layer> | Flow: D0 -> <arm> -> D0

  History (recent):
    <date>: <one-line summary>

  Next Action: <description>
  ```
  If no pending work: "All chain arms are up to date."

Rules:
  [PLAN-01] /sdd-plan MUST be idempotent: unchanged inputs → cache hit, no rescan.
  [PLAN-02] /sdd-plan MUST resolve all @references via INDEX.sdd routing.
  [PLAN-03] /sdd-plan MUST classify prompts to chain arms by keyword matching.
  [PLAN-04] /sdd-plan MUST reference existing artifacts when available.
  [PLAN-05] /sdd-plan MUST output in standard trace format #01-#16.
  [PLAN-06] /sdd-plan MUST include next actionable step in output.
  [PLAN-07] /sdd-plan MUST serve Today's Work, History, and Phase/Layer sections from cache.
  [PLAN-08] Every regeneration MUST bump Revision and append to history.json.
  [PLAN-09] Re-plan on user request is plan-local — no full rescan.
  [PLAN-10] Cache writes are limited to: plan-cache.json, current-plan.sdd, history.json.

